        "C) 1/6",
        "D) 1/12"
      ],
      "correct_option": "C",
      "explanation": "Favorable outcomes = {(1,6),(2,5),(3,4),(4,3),(5,2),(6,1)} = 6. Total = 36. P = 6/36 = 1/6."
    },
    {
      "id": "M25-06",
      "topic": "Relations and Functions",
      "sub_topic": "Relations",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "question": "Let R be a relation on set A = {1, 2, 3} defined by R = {(1,1), (2,2), (3,3), (1,2), (2,1)}. Which property does R have?",
      "options": [
        "A) Reflexive and symmetric",
        "B) Only symmetric",
        "C) Only reflexive",
        "D) Neither reflexive nor symmetric"
      ],
      "correct_option": "A",
      "explanation": "(a,a) for all a\u2208A \u2192 reflexive. If (a,b)\u2208R then (b,a)\u2208R \u2192 symmetric. So R is both."
    },
    {
      "id": "M25-07",
